// SeaM rewrite rules (include/sea/Expr/SeaMRules.hh): one case per rule, each
// checked for soundness with Yices (assumptions => in = out; A-INB only for the
// rules that name it, and with A-INB off no assumption at all), the thesis'
// Fig. 3.3b / 3.4b / 3.5-3.6 examples, and a seeded random test (sound, and a
// normal form: rewriting the result changes nothing), and the provenance of a
// decision (every reason and premise of every leaf pair).
RUN: sea-seam-rules-test 300 | FileCheck %s
REQUIRES: yices
CHECK: test: add-normalize ok
CHECK: test: add-pull-ite ok
CHECK: test: sub ok
CHECK: test: compare ok
CHECK: test: compare-ite ok
CHECK: test: ite-bool ok
CHECK: test: row ok
CHECK: test: thesis-examples ok
CHECK: test: arm ok
CHECK: test: provenance ok
CHECK: test: null ok
CHECK: test: prune-size0 ok
CHECK: random: terms=300
CHECK: random-arm: terms=150
CHECK: failures: 0

